$DIR/main.p:12:10: cannot pass HF(c.get) to call, which keeps it after returning
    HF(c.get) points into a method value whose receiver is in f's frame. A
    method value (at main.p:12) is a record in f's frame that holds its
    receiver, and calling it calls the method on that receiver. call passes s to
    s.String (which may call main.(HF).String) (main.p:9), which stores h in
    package variable keepF (main.p:8), so HF(c.get) would outlive f's frame.
    Go would move this memory to the heap, and its garbage collector would free
    it later. Plutonium has no garbage collector and never moves memory to the
    heap behind the program's back, so that every allocation is visible in the
    code.
    Change call to take a value or an owner, which it can keep: an owned[T] from
    new, a shared[T], or a library owner such as a vec.Vec.
    (see "Views" in the Plutonium spec, section 18.3)
    (run "pluto explain E3003" for a longer explanation)
